Structural changes in fitter code
+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+

_NUMUONLY__ precompiler flag and gOscAnaTypeChoice option are both redundant and conflicting.
The fit parameter list and the list of samples included in the fit is all the information needed to specify the analysis.
Also, we should be able to switch between different analyses without having to recompile our code.
These options need to be added in the analysis XML config file and read by Opt at initialization (so that binnings etc
can be set correctly for each analysis).

--
SuperkDetectorFSI, SuperkDetector and FSI are nearly identical, causing lot of code duplication and many #idfdef blocks.
If SK efficiency and FSI covariance matrices can be added in present analysis (because the binning is identical),
the combined covariance matrix could be handled by SuperkDetector (and FSI disabled). SuperkDetectorFSI is redundant.
Best to keep both SuperkDetector and FSI classes as, in the future, the SK efficiency and FSI covariance matrix 
binning might evolve differently.

--
In SuperkExpectation::TweakSystematic(), is the best_banff option needed?

--
In SuperkExpectation::SetNuisanceParams(), are the all_banff_fit and all_1Re_eff necessary (given that we will 
always fit for all systematics now)?

--
In NuXSec, replace the numerous
  void TweakFermiMom      (double twkdial) { fFermiMomTwkDial      = twkdial; }
  void TweakSpecFunc      (double twkdial) { fSpecFuncTwkDial      = twkdial; }
  void TweakWshape        (double twkdial) { fWshapeTwkDial        = twkdial; }
  void TweakShapeCCoth    (double twkdial) { fShapeCCothTwkDial    = twkdial; }
  void TweakPiLessDelta   (double twkdial) { fPiLessDeltaTwkDial   = twkdial; }
  void TweakBindE         (double twkdial) { fBindETwkDial         = twkdial; }
  void TweakNormCCcoh     (double twkdial) { fNormCCcohTwkDial     = twkdial; }
  ...
  ...
  ...
with a single
  void Tweak(conv::PhysParamId_t p, double twkdial)


